-- erwartet: N311
-- **Lane 194 (`N311`): an axiom call/binding at an empty reason answer.**
--
-- `reason Leer` names no cases: the channel carries no value any answer
-- could take, so binding it binds nothing. The declaration itself parses
-- (an empty case list is grammatical); what falls is the USE, where the
-- missing answer would flow. The twin is a one-case reason, which stays
-- accepted; it is pinned inline (`w1_proben` in `m1.rs` covers the
-- inhabited direction through the syscall probe).
module gift973 {

reason Leer {
}

axiom hol() -> Leer effects { pure } unfalsifiable "probe";

impl fn f() -> u32 effects { pure } costs <= 8 ops {
    let x = hol();
    return 1;
}

}
